From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fiona Ebner <f.ebner@proxmox.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 16:12:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] hw/scsi/lsi53c895a: gracefully handle re-entrant DMA

A re-entrant lsi_do_dma() call might lead to the current request
having residual state, i.e. smaller dma_len than before. While not
clear if this is a reachable scenario in practice, it does not seem
impossible for the current request to be swapped out for a different
one by nested frames. The case where a nested frame would
synchronously complete or cancel a request, was already fixed by
d459131ff5 ("lsi53c895a: keep SCSIRequest alive during DMA"). To fix
the remaining issues, check that the current request is still the same
and skip if not, and shrink the count according to the changed
dma_len.

For details see the Buglink below.

Buglink: https://gitlab.com/qemu-project/qemu/-/work_items/4088
Originally-by: TaeD <kty0730wq@yonsei.ac.kr>
[FE: always re-calculate count if dma_len changes]
Co-developed-by: Thomas Lamprecht <t.lamprecht@proxmox.com>
Signed-off-by: Fiona Ebner <f.ebner@proxmox.com>
---
 hw/scsi/lsi53c895a.c | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hw/scsi/lsi53c895a.c b/hw/scsi/lsi53c895a.c
index 1b7f02fc7c..2e97f99a6a 100644
--- a/hw/scsi/lsi53c895a.c
+++ b/hw/scsi/lsi53c895a.c
@@ -625,6 +625,7 @@ static void lsi_bad_selection(LSIState *s, uint32_t id)
 static void lsi_do_dma(LSIState *s, int out)
 {
     uint32_t count;
+    uint32_t dma_len;
     dma_addr_t addr;
     SCSIDevice *dev;
     SCSIRequest *req;
@@ -645,6 +646,8 @@ static void lsi_do_dma(LSIState *s, int out)
     if (count > p->dma_len)
         count = p->dma_len;
 
+    dma_len = p->dma_len;
+
     addr = s->dnad;
     /* both 40 and Table Indirect 64-bit DMAs store upper bits in dnad64 */
     if (lsi_dma_40bit(s) || lsi_dma_ti64bit(s))
@@ -671,6 +674,27 @@ static void lsi_do_dma(LSIState *s, int out)
         scsi_req_unref(req);
         return;
     }
+
+    /*
+     * The transfer above can re-enter this device through its own MMIO BAR.
+     * Do not apply a pre-transfer snapshot to a different current request,
+     * and re-calculate against residual state consumed by a nested DMA frame.
+     * It's not clear if there is a reachable call sequence that swaps out the
+     * current request in practice, so the first check might just be
+     * defense-in-depth.
+     */
+    if (p != s->current) {
+        scsi_req_unref(req);
+        return;
+    }
+    if (dma_len > p->dma_len) {
+        if (p->dma_len == 0) {
+            /* the nested frame already continued the request */
+            scsi_req_unref(req);
+            return;
+        }
+        count -= MIN(count, dma_len - p->dma_len);
+    }
     scsi_req_unref(req);
 
     p->dma_len -= count;
